(1. Topic Introduction) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Machine Learning enables computer systems to learn patterns and decision boundaries directly from empirical data without) Tj
0 -12 Td
(being explicitly programmed. It spans supervised learning \(labeled targets\), unsupervised clustering, and reinforcement agents.) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -7 Td
/F2 12 Tf
0 -16 Td
(2. Important Concepts) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(- Supervised vs Unsupervised Learning: Regression and classification versus clustering \(K-Means\) and dimensionality reduction \(PCA\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Linear Regression & Cost Functions: Ordinary Least Squares, Mean Squared Error \(MSE\), and Gradient Descent optimization.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Logistic Regression: Sigmoid activation function mapping linear combinations into probabilistic [0, 1] classifications.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Bias-Variance Tradeoff: Underfitting \(high bias, low variance\) versus overfitting \(low bias, high variance\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Model Evaluation Metrics: Precision, Recall, F1-Score, ROC-AUC, Confusion Matrix, and K-Fold Cross-Validation.) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -7 Td
/F2 12 Tf
0 -16 Td
(3. Detailed Explanations) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Supervised models map feature vector X to continuous target Y \(regression\) or categorical class C \(classification\). Optimization) Tj
0 -12 Td
(algorithms like Gradient Descent iteratively update model weights by computing loss function gradients. Regularization techniques) Tj
0 -12 Td
(\(L1 Lasso, L2 Ridge\) penalize excessive parameter magnitudes, preventing overfitting on training datasets.) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -7 Td
/F2 12 Tf
0 -16 Td
