(5. Key Takeaways) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(1. Always split datasets into train, validation, and test subsets to guarantee generalizability on unseen data.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(2. In imbalanced datasets \(e.g. rare fraud or medical diagnoses\), precision, recall, and F1-Score supersede raw accuracy.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(3. Feature scaling \(StandardScaler or MinMaxScaler\) is essential for distance-based and gradient-descent algorithms.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(4. Combat overfitting through cross-validation, regularization, and gathering more representative training samples.) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -7 Td
/F2 12 Tf
0 -16 Td
